title: $:/mf/gen/CLI command/mf order
catalog: CLI command
target: mf order
summary: Number a folder's direct children for sorting: assigns `order_file` / `order_dir` (files and dirs are numbered independently; an existing position is never overwritten), then marks the folder itself `order_numbered = true`. Orders by an ordering metadata, then a shared name pattern, then creation date

!! Reference

```
Number a folder's direct children for sorting: assigns `order_file` / `order_dir` (files and dirs are numbered independently; an existing position is never overwritten), then marks the folder itself `order_numbered = true`. Orders by an ordering metadata, then a shared name pattern, then creation date

Usage: mf order [OPTIONS] <PATH>

Arguments:
  <PATH>
          The folder whose direct children to number

Options:
      --meta <META>
          Metadata field giving an explicit order
          
          [default: mfr_meta_track]

      --max-gap <MAX_GAP>
          Largest gap between shared-pattern name numbers still treated as an order (a larger gap ⇒ the number is an id/hash, ignored)
          
          [default: 1000]

      --dry-run
          Print the planned positions without writing them

  -h, --help
          Print help
```
